              },
              {
                "name": "support",
                "path": "gpui/tests/support",
                "c4_level": "unknown",
                "description": "Fast-UI test support — render a `ReactiveViewModel` in `TestAppContext` without any backend, then query `BoundsRegistry` for layout assertions.",
                "pattern_status": "planned",
                "content": "Fast-UI test support — render a `ReactiveViewModel` in `TestAppContext`\nwithout any backend, then query `BoundsRegistry` for layout assertions.\n\nThis is the L2 primitive from the fast UI test plan (see\n`frontends/gpui/ZED_UI_PATTERNS.md §14`). Production-only concerns\n(reactive engine, DI, tokio runtime, real session) are replaced with a\npanicking stub; fixtures that pull on any of those will fail loudly,\nsignalling that the fixture is outside the pure-layout subset.",
                "source_file": "gpui/tests/support/mod.rs",
                "parent": "gpui",
                "files": [
                  {
                    "name": "mod.rs"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "name": "test_init",
                "path": "gpui/tests/test_init",
                "c4_level": "unknown",
                "description": "Observability init for every windowed (`frontends/gpui/tests/*`) test binary.",
                "pattern_status": "planned",
                "content": "Observability init for every windowed (`frontends/gpui/tests/*`) test\nbinary.\n\nWindowed targets used to install NO tracing subscriber at all, so every\n`warn!`/`error!` a widget, driver or background worker emitted during a test\nwas discarded by `tracing`'s no-op global dispatcher before anything could\nread it. That made the \"falls back VISIBLY\" tier of the error philosophy\nunenforceable here: a degradation could announce itself perfectly and the\nwindowed suite would still be green and silent (a silent-empty context-path\nresolution once survived six rounds of #27 this way).\n\nDeclaring `mod test_init;` in a test file is the whole wiring — the\nconstructor below runs before `main`/the libtest harness, so the subscriber\nis up before any SUT code can emit. `windowed_log_capture.rs` fails the\nsuite if a target forgets the declaration.",
                "source_file": "gpui/tests/test_init/mod.rs",
                "parent": "gpui",
                "files": [
                  {
                    "name": "mod.rs"
                  }
                ]
              }
